# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — repository-root build-context exclusions
# QA finding F8-001 (MINOR): docker-compose builds with `context: ..` (the repo
# root), so without this file the ENTIRE repository — including the large legacy
# DotNetNuke `Library/` and `Website/` trees and `.git/` — is sent to the Docker
# daemon as build context, and a non-pristine working tree can leak host
# `node_modules`/`bin`/`obj` into the images via `COPY backend/`/`COPY frontend/`.
#
# This file keeps the build context minimal and prevents host-artifact
# contamination while preserving every input the Dockerfiles actually COPY
# (backend sources/csproj/Directory.Build.props/global.json, frontend
# sources/package*.json/angular.json/tsconfig*, and docker/nginx.conf).
# Validated against the real working tree: 0 build inputs excluded.
# =============================================================================

# --- Version control & VCS metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
**/.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- .NET build output / intermediates (SDK stage restores & publishes fresh) ---
**/bin
**/obj
**/[Tt]est[Rr]esults
**/*.trx
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.vs

# --- Node / Angular install & build output (build stage runs npm ci + ng build) ---
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular
**/coverage
**/out-tsc

# --- IDE / editor noise ---
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# --- Legacy DotNetNuke source trees: reference-only, never built into the images ---
Library/
Website/

# --- Repo tooling, docs & QA output: not part of either image ---
blitzy/
docs/
*.sln
catalog-info.yaml
mkdocs.yml

# --- Docker metadata itself ---
.dockerignore
